</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.2.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Contains declarative information about the cluster’s desired state.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.2.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Pod Specifications: Resource limits, volumes.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Service Configurations: LoadBalancer, ClusterIP, NodePort.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Networking: Ingress rules, network policies.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Deployments: Replica counts, update strategies.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Secrets/ConfigMaps: Sensitive data and environment configurations.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">RBAC: Roles, bindings.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I2.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I2.i7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I2.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Persistent Storage: PVs, PVCs.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I2.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I2.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.I2.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CronJobs/Jobs: Scheduling, resource allocation.</span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.2.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.3.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.3.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">Ensures system compliance, auditing, and troubleshooting configuration issues.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.2.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T7.2.1.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metrics (Quantitative Data)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.2.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Tracks resource usage and system performance trends.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.2.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Resource Metrics: CPU, memory, disk usage.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Node and Pod Metrics: Resource requests and limits.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Network Metrics: Traffic, latency.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Storage Metrics: PV usage, IOPS.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I3.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I3.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I3.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Application Metrics: Custom KPIs.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I3.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I3.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.I3.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Job Metrics: Success/failure rates, execution times.</span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.2.1.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.4.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.4.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">Enables capacity planning, performance optimization, and identifying over/underutilization.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.2.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T7.2.1.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Security (Audit and Compliance Data)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.2.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Monitors security events and access control changes.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.2.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="A1.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A1.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Audit Logs: API server actions, access logs.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">RBAC Logs: Role/RoleBinding changes.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Pod Security Policies (PSP): Violations, enforcement.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A1.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Network Policies: Logs for unauthorized access attempts.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A1.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A1.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A1.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Vulnerability Scans: Container, pod, and node assessments.</span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.2.1.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.5.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A1.T7.2.1.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">Protects the cluster from security breaches and ensures compliance with security policies.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Appendix A Monitoring Data Types in Kubernetes ‣ KubeIntellect: A Modular LLM-Orchestrated Agent Framework for End-to-End Kubernetes Management" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> provides a comprehensive summary of the key data types used for monitoring and managing Kubernetes clusters. The data is categorized into four distinct groups: <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Logs (Operational Data)</span>, <span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Configurations (Static Data)</span>, <span id="A1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Metrics (Quantitative Data)</span>, and <span id="A1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Security (Audit and Compliance Data)</span>. Each category highlights its focus, key items, and primary purpose within Kubernetes monitoring workflows.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Logs (Operational Data)</span> category captures real-time system activity and runtime issues. This includes system logs (e.g., API server, Scheduler), pod logs for application behavior, and node logs for resource conditions. Key events such as scheduling failures, warnings, and errors like <code id="A1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">ImagePullBackOff</code> or <code id="A1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">CrashLoopBackOff</code> are monitored to provide insights for debugging and tracking system behavior.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Configurations (Static Data)</span> category contains declarative information about the desired state of the cluster. This includes pod specifications, service configurations, and networking setups like ingress rules and network policies. Other critical items, such as Secrets, ConfigMaps, RBAC roles, and persistent storage configurations, are essential for ensuring system compliance, troubleshooting, and auditing.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Metrics (Quantitative Data)</span> category focuses on tracking resource usage and performance trends. Metrics such as CPU, memory, disk usage, and network traffic provide the basis for capacity planning and optimization. Storage metrics, application-specific KPIs, and job execution metrics are also monitored to identify underutilization or bottlenecks.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, the <span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Security (Audit and Compliance Data)</span> category monitors security events and access control changes to protect the cluster from potential breaches. It includes audit logs, RBAC changes, network policy violations, and vulnerability scans. This data ensures compliance with security policies and supports proactive threat detection.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This table serves as a structured guide for understanding the diverse types of monitoring data in Kubernetes, emphasizing their roles in maintaining cluster health, performance, and security.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
</div>
